# Coolify production environment template.
# Leave every value empty in git. Enter the operator values in Coolify, not in this file.
# Do not paste a development .env over these names.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLIC / BUILD-TIME
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Coolify generates these when compose.coolify.yaml is parsed.
# Do not type a Google Cloud IP or a development URL here.
#
# SERVICE_URL_API_8000
#   Source: Coolify domain assigned to the api service, including https://.
#   Used at frontend image build time as VITE_API_BASE_URL.
#   Changing the API domain requires a web image rebuild.
#
# SERVICE_FQDN_API_8000
#   Source: the same API domain, hostname only.
#   Used as TRUSTED_HOSTS.
#
# SERVICE_URL_WEB_80
#   Source: Coolify domain assigned to the web service, including https://.
#   Used as CORS_ORIGINS. It must be the browser origin, not the API origin.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRIVATE / RUNTIME
# Generated by Coolify from the Compose file. Do not replace them with
# development passwords or paste them into the frontend build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# SERVICE_USER_POSTGRES
#   Source: Coolify-generated database user.
# SERVICE_PASSWORD_64_POSTGRES
#   Source: Coolify-generated database password. It is URL-safe.
# SERVICE_PASSWORD_64_SESSION
#   Source: Coolify-generated SESSION_SECRET. Leave it in Coolify.
# POSTGRES_DB
#   Source: operator input. Database name only, not a password.
#   Suggested value: aegisbridge

POSTGRES_DB=

# Cloudflare R2 private bucket. The API, worker, Beat, and migration containers
# receive these. The frontend build does not.
# S3_ENDPOINT_URL example shape: https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# S3_REGION is fixed to auto in compose.coolify.yaml.
# OBJECT_STORAGE_PROVIDER is fixed to r2 in compose.coolify.yaml.

S3_ENDPOINT_URL=
S3_BUCKET=
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL, DISABLED ON FIRST LAUNCH
# Do not set these until the corresponding feature is enabled.
# Threat intelligence sync and Wazuh are fixed off in compose.coolify.yaml.
# Vulnerability intelligence stays enabled and does not need NVD_API_KEY.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# NVD_API_KEY=
# ABUSECH_AUTH_KEY=
# HF_TOKEN=
# BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=
# BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
